{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Good Old Days", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Back in My Day ", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 8, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe events in the news in a range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "secret hideout", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a place where children go to play out of view of parents ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We would meet at our secret hideout.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le08ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use in anecdotes about friendships.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to tease", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to playfully taunt someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We would tease the girls at the corner store.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le08ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "action figure", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small toy in the shape of a person ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We used to play with action figures like G.I. Joe.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le08ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to sing along", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to sing at the same time as a piece of music", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We would listen to and sing along with the songs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le08ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to act out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to recreate a scene or behavior", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Gordie was super at acting out Elvis songs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le08ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to meet up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to meet with someone or some people ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We used to meet up at our secret hiding place.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le08ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to come out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be released", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I think G.I. Joe came out in 1964.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le08ob01aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to pull up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to park beside a place", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: We would usually pull up outside the corner store.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le08ob01aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Used to and Would", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\"> Would </span>and <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> have similar meanings. They are both used to describe something that happened regularly in the past but doesn't happen any longer.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "However, there is an important difference between <span class=\"strong\"> used to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">would</span> .", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\"> Would </span>is not used unless you know that the time frame is in the past, while <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> does not require this. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the following example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">We would visit India every summer <span class=\"strong\">when we were children</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">When we were children</span> refers to a past time frame and therefore makes the meaning of <span class=\"italic\">would</span> clear.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\"> We used to visit India every summer. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I used to go out with a guy before I left for culinary school.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When we were in high school, Ted would write me poems and send me flowers every week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Here, you do not have to include a past time frame since the meaning of <span class=\"italic\">used to</span> is clear.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Phrasal Verbs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " Phrasal verbs consist of a verb and one or more preposition or adverb (called particles). They are common, especially in informal spoken English. The meaning of phrasal verbs is often completely different from the meaning of the verb alone. Phrasal verbs can either be separable or inseparable.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Separable phrasal verbs always require an object.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The object of a phrasal verb can go either between the verb and the preposition or after the preposition.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\"> Examples:</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I handed in my homework.</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I handed my homework in.</span><br/>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If the object of the sentence is a pronoun, it must go between the two parts of the phrasal verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\"> Example:</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I handed it in.</span>\t", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Some phrasal verbs are inseparable, so the verb must be directly followed by its preposition or adverb. Otherwise, the meaning of the phrasal verb will be incorrect.<br/>Some inseparable phrasal verbs never use an object.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\"> Examples:</span><br/> <li> get up = get out of bed   </li> <span class=\"italic\">I get up at seven o'clock every morning.</span><br/><li> take off = leave the ground </li>          <span class=\"italic\">The plane took off on time.</span><br/> <li> look out = beware! be careful!  </li>  <span class=\"italic\">Look out! That car is going to hit you!</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Phrasal Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to meet up\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to meet someone \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to act out\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to recreate a scene or behavior\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to come out\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to be released\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to pull up\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to park beside a place\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to catch up\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"to talk to old friends about old times\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": " We used to meet up at our secret hideout.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He was good at acting out Elvis songs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We would pull up outside the corner store and tease the girls.", "type": "example"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le08ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Interview an older person about their childhood.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask them questions about what they used to do with their friends.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down their answers in English.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Prepare a short report about what they said. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your report to your partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I interv