to play outside. We would meet up at our secret hideout. My friend Teddy used to bring records and we would listen to and sing along with the songs. Gordie, my best friend back then, was super at acting out Elvis songs.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>:  Did you guys use to watch TV at all?<br/>", "id": 2, "time": "22000", "image": "engenn7le08ob01re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">George</span>: Not so much. My parents didn't have a TV until I was about ten years old. My friends and I used to play with action figures like G.I. Joe (I think that came out in 1964). We would ride our bikes all around the neighborhood. We would usually pull up outside the corner store and tease the girls. I haven't talked to Teddy and Gordie in a while. We should catch up!", "id": 3, "time": "46500", "image": "engenn7le08ob01re2img02.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn7le08ob01re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn7le08ob01re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": [], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1}]}]}